# Hermes Sentinel — Stage E9 central service environment file EXAMPLE.
#
# This is a SAFE SYNTHETIC TEMPLATE. An operator copies it to
# /etc/hermes-sentinel/sentinel.env (root:root, 0600) and edits it
# locally on the central host (see docs/SENTINEL_DEPLOYMENT.md).
#
# This is a systemd EnvironmentFile, NOT a shell profile: values are
# plain KEY=value pairs read by the systemd manager, which supplies
# them to the central hermes-sentinel process (E6 settings loading).
# Never write `export ...` here, and never pass a token on a command
# line (it would land in shell history and process listings).
#
# JSON QUOTING BOUNDARY — read this before editing the two JSON values:
# systemd EnvironmentFile parsing removes ONE pair of outer single
# quotes around a whole value. SENTINEL_HOSTS_JSON and
# SENTINEL_NODE_TOKENS_JSON therefore keep their ENTIRE value wrapped
# in single quotes, so the literal JSON double quotes inside reach E6
# intact:
#
#   SENTINEL_HOSTS_JSON='[{"name":"REPLACE_ME",...}]'
#
# Do NOT remove the outer single quotes, do NOT convert the JSON to a
# different configuration format, and do NOT add `export`. E6 remains
# the only parser of these values.
#
# The example values below are deliberately synthetic and deliberately
# NON-RUNNABLE: mandatory placeholders (SENTINEL_LISTEN_PORT,
# SENTINEL_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID, the REPLACE_ME JSON entries and the bot
# token) are INVALID under E6 validation, so an accidentally unedited
# example fails closed during startup BEFORE a usable service runs.
# They are NOT production-valid values. No real token, chat id, server
# IP, domain or host identity belongs in this file.
#
# Optional E6 variables (leave absent when not needed):
#
#   SENTINEL_TELEGRAM_MESSAGE_THREAD_ID
#     Omit entirely to send to a chat without a topic. For the Hermes
#     Telegram topic deployment, set it locally (in the installed
#     sentinel.env copy) to the actual positive topic/thread id. Never
#     commit the real value.
#   SENTINEL_TELEGRAM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
#     Omit to keep the accepted TelegramSettings default (10.0 s).

SENTINEL_DATABASE_PATH=/var/lib/hermes-sentinel/sentinel.sqlite3
SENTINEL_LISTEN_HOST=127.0.0.1
SENTINEL_LISTEN_PORT=REPLACE_ME
SENTINEL_MONITOR_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60
SENTINEL_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1
SENTINEL_HOSTS_JSON='[{"name":"REPLACE_ME","heartbeat":{"expected_interval_seconds":60,"stale_after_seconds":180},"external":{"tcp_host":"REPLACE_ME.invalid","tcp_port":443}}]'
SENTINEL_NODE_TOKENS_JSON='{"REPLACE_ME":"REPLACE_WITH_UNIQUE_NODE_TOKEN"}'
SENTINEL_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
SENTINEL_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=REPLACE_ME
